WEBVTT

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.610
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.410
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.415 --> 00:00:21.221
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:28.866
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:28.869 --> 00:00:33.202
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.584 --> 00:00:35.050
But, with you...

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.168
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:39.016 --> 00:00:42.720
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:47.440
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.820
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.400
Just to survive!

00:00:53.602 --> 00:00:55.360
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.200
Take this moment...

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.854
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:00.854 --> 00:01:03.030
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.903
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:04.903 --> 00:01:08.580
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.710
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.420
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.090
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.260
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.090
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:24.039
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:39.490
We five members of Q class were
assigned a case from DDS...

00:01:39.782 --> 00:01:45.413
...to investigate the mysterious disappearance of seven
people within the last decade from Kamikakushi village.

00:01:45.746 --> 00:01:47.623
Therefore, we came to this mountain village.

00:01:49.917 --> 00:01:53.963
We stayed at the old inn, Ryouzanpaku...

00:01:54.088 --> 00:01:57.592
...along with a TV crew, to investigate legends
of the old Japanese army's treasure.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:01.345
The day after our arrival, we discovered
the body of the reporter...

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:04.015
...Azegami Rio-san, who mysteriously
disappeared.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.977
To solve the mystery behind these
mysterious disappearances...

00:02:08.352 --> 00:02:11.230
...Kyuu, Kinta and Kazuma remained
in Hyoutan Village...

00:02:11.689 --> 00:02:15.026
...while Ryu-kun and I went
to Kamikakushi village.

00:02:17.945 --> 00:02:23.075
But then the director, Kunihiko Anzai-san,
mysteriously disappeared...

00:02:23.451 --> 00:02:28.998
...leaving only a strange video recording
of his abduction into the air.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:40.343
Look, that pile of twigs.

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:43.387
That's where Director Anzai
was abducted into the air!

00:02:44.805 --> 00:02:46.849
So this is the obstacle he was talking about.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:48.142
Probably.

00:02:50.519 --> 00:02:55.775
But there's nothing here that looks like it
could be used to hang a person from.

00:02:57.693 --> 00:02:58.402
I see.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.029
Ryu-kun?

00:03:00.571 --> 00:03:02.907
There are three hints to solve this
mysterious disappearance.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:08.829
The first is the sound you could faintly hear
when Anzai-san was abducted into the air.

00:03:09.038 --> 00:03:09.538
Sound?

00:03:10.748 --> 00:03:11.874
Listen carefully.

00:03:16.253 --> 00:03:18.214
You're right, I can hear something.

00:03:18.714 --> 00:03:21.300
The second hint is this stake that you can see...

00:03:22.134 --> 00:03:25.513
...right as he was abducted, when the flashlight
illuminated it for a split second.

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:28.432
This is a stake used to pull
a rope across a rice field.

00:03:29.225 --> 00:03:32.186
But, it doesn't look as if there
are any stakes in this area.

00:03:33.437 --> 00:03:39.318
And the third hint is this location that you found.

00:03:40.277 --> 00:03:40.987
That means...

00:03:41.278 --> 00:03:43.531
Yes, this wasn't a mysterious disappearance.

00:03:44.448 --> 00:03:47.576
It was a trap designed to lure Director
Anzai with hints to the treasure...

00:03:48.077 --> 00:03:50.871
...and launching him into the air to be killed.

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.082
This mysterious disappearance is a trick!

00:03:53.708 --> 00:03:55.960
Even if it is a trick, just how was it done?

00:03:56.293 --> 00:03:57.586
listen to this sound again.

00:04:01.799 --> 00:04:04.802
I see, it's the sound of a tractor's engine.

00:04:05.553 --> 00:04:10.182
Right, the perpetrator used a tractor
to pull Anzai-san into the air.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.727
The perpetrator probably set
up a trap on the footpath...

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:16.731
...waited for the moment he stopped
to get past the obstacle...

00:04:17.064 --> 00:04:19.108
...and pulled the wire with the tractor.

00:04:19.984 --> 00:04:21.360
I figured you'd get it.

00:04:22.319 --> 00:04:24.155
The stake in the video was the trap.

00:04:24.989 --> 00:04:28.826
It was probably there to keep the mechanism
for tightening the wire close to the ground.

00:04:30.286 --> 00:04:34.373
I guess this obstacle made of little
twigs was part of the trap as well.

00:04:36.292 --> 00:04:38.127
But what did the perpetrator use as a pivot?

00:04:38.669 --> 00:04:43.382
True, there are no buildings tall
enough to hang someone from.

00:04:44.341 --> 00:04:46.510
But if you look around the area you'll see it...

00:04:47.011 --> 00:04:48.596
look, there and there.

00:04:48.971 --> 00:04:50.264
The two telephone poles...

00:04:50.681 --> 00:04:51.432
You mean...

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:52.349
Right.

00:04:53.017 --> 00:04:56.562
let's say these two twigs are those two posts.

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:59.940
And this 5 yen coin is a person.

00:05:01.108 --> 00:05:05.279
You place a thin but strong wire
across these two posts.

00:05:07.031 --> 00:05:12.787
If you pull one end with a tractor, the force on
the wire is enough to pull someone into the air.

00:05:13.454 --> 00:05:14.288
Like this.

00:05:17.208 --> 00:05:20.294
The perpetrator probably put on a
mask, and posing as a villager...

00:05:20.836 --> 00:05:24.882
...Lured Anzai-san here with fake
information about the treasure.

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:31.263
And when Anzai-san moved past the obstacle
and put his foot into the wire...

00:05:40.523 --> 00:05:44.318
Anzai-san was dropped, upside down,
from a height of ten meters.

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:45.945
He probably died instantaneously.

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:49.698
His landing point is probably
between those two posts.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:51.158
So, right there.

00:05:51.826 --> 00:05:55.121
There's traces of blood. You can see that
someone put dirt over it to hide it.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.248
It looks like there's no doubt.

00:05:57.706 --> 00:05:59.416
What a horrible trick.

00:06:00.084 --> 00:06:03.671
Who is this perpetrator that keeps committing
these horrible murders?

00:06:05.589 --> 00:06:09.385
Megu, let's return to the inn and ask someone
who knows this village to help us.

00:06:13.222 --> 00:06:14.473
What did you say?

00:06:14.765 --> 00:06:16.725
No way, even Anzai-san...

00:06:17.184 --> 00:06:20.146
Let's ask the villagers to help
us search for the body.

00:06:20.396 --> 00:06:22.356
I'm sure that the body was hidden
somewhere close by.

00:06:22.356 --> 00:06:23.774
That won't be necessary.

00:06:24.733 --> 00:06:25.568
Oowada-san...

00:06:25.693 --> 00:06:28.904
I'm sorry, but I overheard what
you guys were talking about...

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:30.865
...and I checked a spot that came to mind.

00:06:31.699 --> 00:06:32.575
And then...

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:36.912
Is that true?

00:06:37.079 --> 00:06:41.000
It looks like the words of the high
priest have become a reality.

00:06:41.208 --> 00:06:42.001
Kurozumi-san...

00:06:42.626 --> 00:06:46.422
Oowada-san, a former believer
such as yourself should know...

00:06:46.964 --> 00:06:48.966
...what happens if you walk around
this village without a mask...

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:53.137
...or if you violate Ekigami-sama‘s
sacred domains.

00:06:53.721 --> 00:06:54.722
You were a believer once?

00:06:54.722 --> 00:06:55.973
Oowada, you...

00:06:57.641 --> 00:07:02.104
If you don't wish to be a "mysterious
disappearance", return to us.

00:07:03.189 --> 00:07:07.318
If you go through the training again and
beg for forgiveness, you might be saved.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:08.611
Ridiculous.

00:07:09.695 --> 00:07:12.823
Neither the murder of the reporter nor this
case were a mysterious disappearance.

00:07:13.532 --> 00:07:15.659
They were both crimes committed
using clever tricks.

00:07:16.452 --> 00:07:17.620
R-Ryu-kun...

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:25.085
Furthermore, if the Ekishin religion is involved, your
revered high priest might be the perpetrator.

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:27.171
How dare you speak like that!

00:07:28.088 --> 00:07:32.801
The high priest is always within his sacred temple,
behind the wall, where no commoner is allowed.

00:07:33.344 --> 00:07:36.222
And he has never left this Kamikakushi village.

00:07:37.097 --> 00:07:40.726
That's why there's no way that he could be the
perpetrator of the crime in Hyoutan village.

00:07:41.101 --> 00:07:43.145
He might have snuck out.

00:07:43.771 --> 00:07:46.815
There are guards 24/7 at the checkpoint
outside the tunnel.

00:07:47.149 --> 00:07:49.944
Besides, the high priest has never
gone through the tunnel.

00:07:50.444 --> 00:07:53.030
He might have pretended to be someone else.

00:07:53.781 --> 00:07:58.118
In the first place, have you ever
seen the face behind the mask?

00:07:58.494 --> 00:08:04.166
No, but there's a log of who passed
through the checkpoint and when.

00:08:05.125 --> 00:08:08.796
Using your lingo, it's easy to determine
if the high priest has an alibi or not.

00:08:09.296 --> 00:08:13.259
And there's no way the high priest would pretend to
be a different person to get through the checkpoint!

00:08:18.430 --> 00:08:20.182
Ryu-kun, don't you think you overdid it?

00:08:22.142 --> 00:08:23.477
I just taunted him.

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:25.479
I'm anxious to see how he reacts.

00:08:38.242 --> 00:08:39.076
How are things going, Kazuma?

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:40.995
Any progress on breaking the cypher?

00:08:41.495 --> 00:08:43.163
You can tell by the look on my face.

00:08:43.539 --> 00:08:44.707
You still haven't found the answer...

00:08:45.207 --> 00:08:48.127
Well, if my theory is correct, the
simple explanation would be...

00:08:48.127 --> 00:08:52.006
...that each number corresponds to
a letter in the Japanese alphabet.

00:08:52.339 --> 00:08:54.258
See how there's numbers from 1-48?

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:58.762
The alphabet only has 26 letters, and
Korean Hangul only has 24 letters.

00:08:59.305 --> 00:09:04.893
In Thai, there are 44 consonants, 32
vowels and 4 phonetic nuances...

00:09:05.144 --> 00:09:07.062
...so the numbers would have been higher.

00:09:07.896 --> 00:09:11.734
I always think this, but you're a
really weird grade schooler.

00:09:12.192 --> 00:09:13.193
What's more, look here.

00:09:13.402 --> 00:09:16.947
There are places here and there that have
numbers in parentheses and in circles.

00:09:17.573 --> 00:09:19.575
These are probably the sonants
and lowercase letters.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.286
If you've figured out that much, doesn't
it mean that you've basically solved it?

00:09:22.453 --> 00:09:27.458
I thought so and tried pairing each letter
of the alphabet with a number.

00:09:27.708 --> 00:09:29.376
But that didn't work.

00:09:29.877 --> 00:09:32.504
So I was trying to think of another solution,
but my head's just spinning.

00:09:33.172 --> 00:09:37.468
That's another bad habit of
yours; you think too hard.

00:09:37.801 --> 00:09:38.927
Here let me try.

00:09:39.928 --> 00:09:42.765
I have the most flexible mind at DDS.

00:09:43.265 --> 00:09:44.558
Just leave it to me.

00:09:45.142 --> 00:09:48.020
Let's see, you move around
the screen with this thing...

00:09:50.689 --> 00:09:53.025
What? There's something
written here in Japanese.

00:09:53.025 --> 00:09:53.734
Hold on!

00:09:54.234 --> 00:09:55.069
What's that?

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:57.946
This is a classified document, handle with care.

00:09:59.448 --> 00:10:02.409
That's old Japanese isn't it?

00:10:02.868 --> 00:10:04.787
Yeah, it is a document written during the war.

00:10:04.787 --> 00:10:05.954
Old Japanese?

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:07.915
I got it, it's the I-ro-ha!

00:10:08.248 --> 00:10:08.999
I-ro-ha?

00:10:09.124 --> 00:10:10.000
Kinta, move.

00:10:10.793 --> 00:10:11.377
Okay...

00:10:12.544 --> 00:10:15.631
You were right, Kinta, I was thinking too hard.

00:10:16.131 --> 00:10:19.176
Number 1 is i; 2 is re; 3 is ha; 4 is mi.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:20.844
Deciphered!

00:10:22.596 --> 00:10:23.347
Just like I thought!

00:10:23.472 --> 00:10:27.518
They didn't use the 'aiueo' alphabet, they used
the 'iroha' order to create this cipher!

00:10:28.227 --> 00:10:29.478
What, you gotta be kidding...

00:10:29.937 --> 00:10:30.646
What's wrong?

00:10:30.979 --> 00:10:31.772
Look at this.

00:10:32.147 --> 00:10:32.815
What?

00:10:33.023 --> 00:10:35.150
Oh, nice! It's all hiragana and easy to read.

00:10:35.484 --> 00:10:37.611
I can read hiragana best.

00:10:37.945 --> 00:10:39.780
Who cares about that? Just read it!

00:10:39.822 --> 00:10:42.616
Yeah, yeah. Hmm, what's this?

00:10:42.991 --> 00:10:45.369
The Grand Imperial Army of Japan has...

00:10:45.661 --> 00:10:48.747
...as a last resort against the allied
forces of America and Britain... ..

00:10:48.747 --> 00:10:51.458
...begun the development of biological weapons.

00:10:51.458 --> 00:10:53.127
Beginning with the strengthening of Housou.

00:10:53.127 --> 00:10:53.710
Housou?

00:10:54.044 --> 00:10:54.753
Housou is?

00:10:55.129 --> 00:10:56.630
Hey, it means smallpox.

00:10:56.922 --> 00:10:58.006
There's no doubt.

00:10:58.465 --> 00:11:01.885
The old Japanese army researched
smallpox here.

00:11:02.803 --> 00:11:04.471
<i>Research on smallpox...</i>

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:10.436
Smallpox is the strongest and
most lethal virus out there.

00:11:10.436 --> 00:11:14.189
Currently, there are still researchers in several countries
attempting to use smallpox as a biological weapon.

00:11:15.023 --> 00:11:17.484
Then the old Japanese army's treasure is....

00:11:19.778 --> 00:11:22.865
Excuse me, there's a phone call from
Ryu-san in Kamikakushi village...

00:11:23.699 --> 00:11:24.783
Thanks, Mio-san!

00:11:26.952 --> 00:11:28.078
Ryu, did something happen?

00:11:28.829 --> 00:11:31.457
We've found the body of Director Anzai who was
a victim of another mysterious disappearance.

00:11:31.582 --> 00:11:32.207
What?

00:11:32.291 --> 00:11:34.168
The mysterious disappearance
was a clever trick.

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:37.212
I don't think we'll find the perpetrator
using normal methods.

00:11:37.713 --> 00:11:39.965
I see, we found something amazing out as well.

00:11:40.466 --> 00:11:44.845
The old Japanese army apparently did
research on biological weapons...

00:11:44.887 --> 00:11:47.514
...here in Hyoutan village
and Kamikakushi village.

00:11:47.681 --> 00:11:48.724
Biological weapons?

00:11:49.224 --> 00:11:50.267
You mean smallpox?

00:11:50.934 --> 00:11:51.810
Say, Ryu...

00:11:52.478 --> 00:11:54.521
The masks of Ekishin believers depict smallpox.

00:11:54.855 --> 00:11:56.565
The biological weapon was smallpox.

00:11:57.065 --> 00:11:59.485
Do you think Ekishin is involved in these cases?

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:01.528
I think that's the natural conclusion.

00:12:02.529 --> 00:12:04.865
In any case contact the police right away and...

00:12:05.532 --> 00:12:07.326
...have them come to Kamikakushi
village immediately.

00:12:08.869 --> 00:12:09.495
Ryu-kun...

00:12:17.836 --> 00:12:18.587
What happened?

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:19.296
Ryu!

00:12:19.421 --> 00:12:20.047
Ryu!

00:12:21.757 --> 00:12:22.424
Ryu...

00:12:23.651 --> 00:12:24.318
Megu...

00:12:31.242 --> 00:12:34.370
Ryu-kun, what's going to happen to us?

00:12:34.995 --> 00:12:35.830
No need to worry.

00:12:36.705 --> 00:12:40.793
Their masks are a bit creepy, but I don't think they
are the kind to resort to unnecessary violence.

00:12:41.127 --> 00:12:42.628
What the hell do you guys want?

00:12:42.628 --> 00:12:44.034
Its the people from the TV station.

00:12:43.121 --> 00:12:44.421
Take that damn mask off!

00:12:44.672 --> 00:12:45.673
Please calm down.

00:12:46.132 --> 00:12:48.801
If we stay calm, these people won't do anything.

00:12:49.093 --> 00:12:49.927
Shut your trap!

00:12:50.052 --> 00:12:52.138
You're one of them too, aren't you, Oowada?

00:12:52.263 --> 00:12:53.013
Be quiet!

00:12:53.806 --> 00:12:54.890
This is sacred land.

00:12:55.558 --> 00:12:56.976
This is the temple of our high priest.

00:12:57.935 --> 00:12:58.727
Kurozumi-san...

00:13:00.229 --> 00:13:01.897
What are you going to do to us?

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:07.194
You will stand before a hearing
with our high priest.

00:13:07.903 --> 00:13:08.779
A hearing?

00:13:27.882 --> 00:13:29.758
We've been waiting for you, high priest.

00:13:32.052 --> 00:13:37.892
There was a report that these people were
walking around the village without masks.

00:13:38.434 --> 00:13:40.519
Please let us know your decision.

00:13:43.397 --> 00:13:44.273
Sign language?

00:13:46.984 --> 00:13:48.068
Understood.

00:13:50.696 --> 00:13:52.781
I will proclaim the words of the high priest.

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:56.911
You will leave Kamikakushi village immediately.

00:13:57.328 --> 00:13:59.246
That's the high priest's decision.

00:13:59.622 --> 00:14:01.373
Otherwise, even more horrible...

00:14:01.373 --> 00:14:02.750
Yeah, right?

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:07.880
Do you think I can leave without filming a show
after two members of my team were killed?

00:14:08.339 --> 00:14:12.635
Now it's not about the treasure; this will be
a battle to avenge Anzai and Azegami!

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:17.890
I swear on my career as a TV man that I'm going
to find out the truth behind your Ekishin religion!

00:14:18.265 --> 00:14:19.475
This piece of shit!

00:14:20.017 --> 00:14:22.811
We're going back to Hyoutan village
and making our plans!

00:14:23.354 --> 00:14:24.063
Iwashimizu-san...

00:14:31.153 --> 00:14:32.196
Is that so?

00:14:32.321 --> 00:14:34.823
Kurozumi-san, what did the high priest just say?

00:14:35.282 --> 00:14:39.870
It is a sad thing, but there will be yet another
mysterious disappearance in Hyoutan village.

00:14:44.583 --> 00:14:45.292
High priest...

00:14:45.793 --> 00:14:49.755
Why do you wear a mask and gloves and
only communicate in sign language?

00:14:50.089 --> 00:14:51.257
How dare you talk to our high priest like that?

00:14:51.715 --> 00:14:52.716
I'll be straight forward.

00:14:53.342 --> 00:14:57.137
I think you're the perpetrator
of the two murders.

00:14:57.846 --> 00:14:58.597
Such insolence...

00:14:58.722 --> 00:15:00.182
He actually said it...

00:15:00.683 --> 00:15:03.394
The murder of Director Anzai
in Kamikakushi village...

00:15:04.061 --> 00:15:09.400
...and the murder of reporter Azegami in Hyoutan
village were not impossible for you to do.

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:13.779
Nobody knows your face or your voice.

00:15:14.238 --> 00:15:19.743
I believe that you could easily disguise
yourself as someone in this village...

00:15:20.327 --> 00:15:21.912
...go through the tunnel...

00:15:22.162 --> 00:15:23.747
...commit the crime...

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:26.250
...and come back through the tunnel again.

00:15:26.834 --> 00:15:32.381
As I have already said, there is a log
of all who pass through the tunnel.

00:15:32.923 --> 00:15:36.802
I checked the logs after that incident
but there were no suspicious entries.

00:15:39.096 --> 00:15:39.722
<i>Yes...</i>

00:15:41.181 --> 00:15:41.807
<i>Yes...</i>

00:15:42.057 --> 00:15:42.683
I understand.

00:15:44.226 --> 00:15:46.020
The high priest says...

00:15:46.645 --> 00:15:47.896
"If you question my integrity...

00:15:48.272 --> 00:15:53.402
...stay at the checkpoint and stand
guard for as long as you wish."

00:15:54.194 --> 00:15:58.615
"I will be returning to the shrine and will
not exit the building behind this wall."

00:15:59.033 --> 00:16:04.455
"But, someone will definitely
die by an act of god."

00:16:06.165 --> 00:16:07.416
A-Again?

00:16:23.432 --> 00:16:24.641
They're still not answering?

00:16:24.683 --> 00:16:26.977
Yeah, I get the same result time after time.

00:16:27.102 --> 00:16:29.688
Damn, what happened to Ryu and Mega?

00:16:30.856 --> 00:16:33.525
Damn, don't think that was
the last you'll see of me.

00:16:33.609 --> 00:16:35.736
Please calm down, Producer Iwashimizu.

00:16:35.861 --> 00:16:36.987
Iwashimizu-san...

00:16:38.238 --> 00:16:40.699
Kagami-san, what happened
at Kamikakushi village?

00:16:40.866 --> 00:16:46.163
He's completely outraged because we were kicked
out of the village by the Ekishin high priest.

00:16:46.580 --> 00:16:49.625
Our producer's impossible to deal
with once he gets like that.

00:16:49.708 --> 00:16:50.709
You were kicked out?

00:16:51.293 --> 00:16:52.378
What about Ryu and Megu?

00:16:53.045 --> 00:16:54.505
Weren't you all kicked out?

00:16:55.005 --> 00:16:58.092
Your two friends stayed back
in Kamikakushi village.

00:17:01.303 --> 00:17:02.012
Why?

00:17:02.471 --> 00:17:05.808
Because Amakusa-sama called
the high priest a murderer...

00:17:06.225 --> 00:17:09.978
...they were allowed to watch the
tunnel until they had enough.

00:17:10.979 --> 00:17:12.147
Such a silly things

00:17:13.148 --> 00:17:14.817
W-Welcome back.

00:17:15.192 --> 00:17:18.779
Mio-san, will you go to Kamikakushi
village later today in my stead?

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:23.242
I was told by the high priest to stay here and
witness the mysterious disappearance.

00:17:23.867 --> 00:17:24.868
Y-Yes.

00:17:25.536 --> 00:17:27.913
Hey, what do you mean by witness?

00:17:28.247 --> 00:17:30.290
It was a revelation by the high priest.

00:17:30.666 --> 00:17:32.793
There will be yet another mysterious
disappearance in this village.

00:17:36.255 --> 00:17:38.382
Hey, those were murders.

00:17:38.799 --> 00:17:42.302
He said it as if those mysterious
disappearances were natural.

00:17:44.179 --> 00:17:44.805
Excuse me.

00:17:45.806 --> 00:17:48.308
Is there something I could do to help?

00:17:48.767 --> 00:17:50.769
I'm worried about Ryu-san and Megu-san too.

00:17:51.145 --> 00:17:54.648
I could let you know how they are doing
once I get to Kamikakushi village.

00:17:55.357 --> 00:17:56.150
Really?

00:17:56.733 --> 00:17:57.734
Thank you, Mio-san!

00:18:02.656 --> 00:18:06.660
No one's gone by since Kurozumi-san
left for Hyoutan village.

00:18:07.035 --> 00:18:07.703
Yeah.

00:18:08.162 --> 00:18:13.333
But what is he thinking? Allowing us to remain and
stand watch over the tunnel for as long as we want.

00:18:13.792 --> 00:18:16.503
If the high priest really is the
perpetrator as you suggest...

00:18:16.837 --> 00:18:20.591
...he cannot kill anyone in Hyoutan
village unless he passes this point.

00:18:21.341 --> 00:18:22.593
That's his goal.

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:25.721
If there should be a third murder...

00:18:26.346 --> 00:18:29.975
...as long as we are here, the
high priest will have an alibi.

00:18:30.517 --> 00:18:35.397
So, the high priest intends to make us his alibi?

00:18:36.023 --> 00:18:36.899
Most likely.

00:18:37.357 --> 00:18:41.528
But how is he going to commit a murder in
Hyoutan village without passing through here?

00:18:42.571 --> 00:18:43.322
Someone's coming!

00:18:44.865 --> 00:18:46.366
It's Mio-san, from the inn.

00:18:46.825 --> 00:18:49.495
You're right, I didn't recognize her because
she isn't wearing her kimono.

00:18:52.039 --> 00:18:52.873
Hello.

00:18:53.207 --> 00:18:55.709
Hi, what's up Mio-san?

00:18:56.418 --> 00:19:00.672
Kyuu-san and the others wanted me
to check how you guys are doing.

00:19:01.215 --> 00:19:02.007
They did?

00:19:02.508 --> 00:19:05.093
They are all very worried about you.

00:19:05.177 --> 00:19:07.262
Oh, this is a little something for you.

00:19:09.765 --> 00:19:10.474
Thanks.

00:19:11.433 --> 00:19:16.522
Mio-san, dressed like that you look
more like a normal high schooler.

00:19:18.774 --> 00:19:20.609
Y-You think so?

00:19:21.109 --> 00:19:22.778
W-Well then I'm off!

00:19:25.489 --> 00:19:28.575
Ryu-kun, Mio-san just blushed again.

00:19:28.742 --> 00:19:29.368
Megu...

00:19:31.245 --> 00:19:34.414
Hey Kyuu, let's go back to our rooms.

00:19:34.581 --> 00:19:37.042
We can hear the phone from there too.

00:19:37.084 --> 00:19:39.086
It's alright Kazuma, you can head back.

00:19:39.253 --> 00:19:43.006
But isn't Mio-san taking a bit
too long to contact us?

00:19:43.382 --> 00:19:44.758
It's already 11:00.

00:19:45.801 --> 00:19:48.345
You don't think that Mio-san got attacked
by the Ekishin people too?

00:19:48.554 --> 00:19:51.014
Kazuma, don't say stuff like that!

00:19:53.225 --> 00:19:53.934
What's wrong?

00:19:54.226 --> 00:19:56.937
Nothing, I just had the feeling
that someone's outside.

00:19:57.145 --> 00:19:58.355
At this time of day?

00:19:58.564 --> 00:19:59.523
I'll go take a look.

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:02.901
Who's there?

00:20:03.485 --> 00:20:06.363
I know you're there, no need
to hide! Come out already!

00:20:09.074 --> 00:20:09.157
Good evening.

00:20:09.199 --> 00:20:10.450
Good evening.

00:20:12.035 --> 00:20:13.996
Geez, it's just the lady from the inn.

00:20:15.247 --> 00:20:18.125
But what are you doing, walking around
with such a dangerous thing?

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:21.253
What did you think? Just preparing breakfast.

00:20:21.378 --> 00:20:21.962
Yes.

00:20:23.547 --> 00:20:27.676
I'm sorry that it took me so long. I'm in the
lobby of the branch house right now.

00:20:29.136 --> 00:20:30.762
Well more importantly, how are Ryu and Megu?

00:20:32.055 --> 00:20:32.764
Guarding?

00:20:33.265 --> 00:20:35.017
Oh, the thing Kurozumi-san mentioned

00:20:35.559 --> 00:20:39.146
Yes, they said they're bored because
nobody would come by for hours.

00:20:39.271 --> 00:20:41.815
I see, so they're okay. That's great.

00:20:43.025 --> 00:20:43.650
Yeah.

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:48.071
That abduction into the air
was done using a wire?

00:20:48.905 --> 00:20:51.408
What a scary trick!

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:54.620
And how was Anzai-san's body discovered?

00:20:55.078 --> 00:20:57.247
The body was found by the camera
man, Oowada-san.

00:20:57.289 --> 00:21:00.125
He said that he searched a
place that came to mind.

00:21:00.542 --> 00:21:01.501
Oowada-san?

00:21:02.169 --> 00:21:05.088
He isn't even from the village, how did
he have an idea where it might be?

00:21:10.093 --> 00:21:12.596
He used to be an Ekishin believer.

00:21:13.096 --> 00:21:15.724
His appearance changed so I didn't
realize it for a long time...

00:21:15.891 --> 00:21:18.602
...but three years ago he used to
live in the neighboring village.

00:21:20.187 --> 00:21:22.189
Hmm, I see.

00:21:35.243 --> 00:21:40.540
So did you know about the assistant,
Kagami-san as well?

00:21:40.957 --> 00:21:41.583
<i>Yes...</i>

00:21:41.583 --> 00:21:46.004
I don't know if it was to check this place out before the
shoot, but she has come to the village a few times.

00:21:46.588 --> 00:21:47.255
I see.

00:21:49.424 --> 00:21:50.175
What was that noise?

00:21:50.509 --> 00:21:52.010
I think it was from the back, on the second floor.

00:21:52.386 --> 00:21:53.011
Let's go?!

00:21:54.221 --> 00:21:55.889
Kyuu-san, did something happen?

00:21:56.098 --> 00:21:57.724
Sorry, Mio-san. I'll call you back.

00:21:59.685 --> 00:22:00.435
That noise...

00:22:00.644 --> 00:22:02.187
It was from Iwashimizu-san's room.

00:22:06.525 --> 00:22:07.275
Iwashimizu-san!

00:22:07.776 --> 00:22:08.902
Did something happen?

00:22:09.236 --> 00:22:10.487
Producer Iwashimizu...

00:22:18.286 --> 00:22:19.162
Iwashimizu-san?

00:22:28.922 --> 00:22:30.132
N-No way...

00:22:30.132 --> 00:22:31.550
Producer Iwashimizu...

00:22:31.758 --> 00:22:33.009
Single strike with a kitchen knife.

00:22:33.218 --> 00:22:34.469
So it did happen after all.

00:22:35.095 --> 00:22:38.724
So this is the mysterious disappearance
that the high priest spoke of.

00:22:39.599 --> 00:22:42.602
It looks like Iwashimizu-san is the victim
of the mysterious disappearance.

00:22:42.644 --> 00:22:43.311
Knock it off!

00:22:43.895 --> 00:22:47.441
How can you say a person with a knife in his chest
is the victim of a "mysterious disappearance"?

00:22:47.899 --> 00:22:49.276
What kind of religion is...

00:22:49.443 --> 00:22:50.569
Let it be, Kinta.

00:22:55.574 --> 00:22:59.119
It's not like we'll find out the
truth if we yell at people.

00:23:00.078 --> 00:23:02.581
The only thing we should do is use
this anger against the perpetrator.

00:23:04.458 --> 00:23:05.125
Kyuu...

00:23:05.917 --> 00:23:08.003
Damn it! I feel so frustrated!

00:23:08.795 --> 00:23:12.507
We came here to find the truth to this case
so no other murders would happen again.

00:23:13.800 --> 00:23:16.887
This kind of brutal murder happens
right in front of us...

00:23:17.387 --> 00:23:19.723
...and we don't even have an idea
who the perpetrator might be!

00:23:21.224 --> 00:23:23.935
But I will never give up.

00:23:24.895 --> 00:23:29.483
I will find the real perpetrator so that
there won't be any more victims!

00:23:30.442 --> 00:23:33.487
Because if a detective gives up, the
case will remain unsolved forever!

00:23:37.332 --> 00:23:40.554
The Sun is setting in a red glow...

00:23:41.184 --> 00:23:43.675
...as it follows me.

00:23:44.020 --> 00:23:46.857
Along this deserted beach...

00:23:46.860 --> 00:23:50.783
...I walk alone once more.

00:23:50.796 --> 00:23:54.165
I can't continue to hold in...

00:23:54.817 --> 00:23:57.152
...the tears that should pour out.

00:23:57.786 --> 00:24:00.257
Why have these memories...

00:24:00.259 --> 00:24:03.789
...become so wonderful?

00:24:04.360 --> 00:24:09.356
Ah... Like an ocean wave, I return to you...

00:24:09.606 --> 00:24:12.129
...because I'm so in love.

00:24:12.860 --> 00:24:15.846
And, now my heart...

00:24:15.851 --> 00:24:17.990
...is heavy with pain.

00:24:18.944 --> 00:24:21.884
Reflections of a bright rainbow...

00:24:21.987 --> 00:24:26.147
...shine on the distant shores of yesturday.

00:24:26.493 --> 00:24:30.118
I'll never forget those days...

00:24:30.125 --> 00:24:35.211
...and I long to see you again.

00:24:37.493 --> 00:24:39.787
The serial murders that are said to
be mysterious disappearances.

00:24:40.079 --> 00:24:42.164
The secret behind the trick that
made those murders possible.

00:24:42.790 --> 00:24:45.459
Q Class solves the difficult question
after their earnest investigation.

00:24:46.085 --> 00:24:49.505
We finally discover the final mystery of this village.

00:24:50.005 --> 00:24:52.925
And the surprising identity of the perpetrator is...

00:24:53.675 --> 00:24:54.551
There's only one answer!

00:24:58.680 --> 00:24:59.556
It's me, Nanami.

00:24:59.932 --> 00:25:02.810
Did you find me this week as well?

00:25:03.352 --> 00:25:04.395
The answer is...

00:25:07.981 --> 00:25:09.191
Were you able to find me?

00:25:09.566 --> 00:25:11.193
Look again next week too!
